---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="QR Code Generator — Free Online QR Code Maker"
    description="Generate free QR codes online. Enter any text or URL, customize size, and download as PNG. No signup required."
>
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-3">QR Code Generator</h1>
        <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
            Enter any text or URL below and generate a QR code instantly.
            Download it as a PNG image.
        </p>

        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg border border-gray-200">
            <label for="qr-input" class="block text-sm font-medium mb-2"
                >Text or URL</label
            >
            <input
                id="qr-input"
                type="text"
                value="https://example.com"
                class="w-full p-3 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500"
                placeholder="Enter text or URL..."
            />

            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 mt-4">
                <div>
                    <label for="qr-size" class="block text-sm font-medium mb-2"
                        >Size (px)</label
                    >
                    <select
                        id="qr-size"
                        class="w-full p-3 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500"
                    >
                        <option value="200">200 x 200</option>
                        <option value="300" selected>300 x 300</option>
                        <option value="400">400 x 400</option>
                        <option value="500">500 x 500</option>
                    </select>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <label for="qr-level" class="block text-sm font-medium mb-2"
                        >Error Correction</label
                    >
                    <select
                        id="qr-level"
                        class="w-full p-3 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500"
                    >
                        <option value="L">Low (L)</option>
                        <option value="M" selected>Medium (M)</option>
                        <option value="Q">Quartile (Q)</option>
                        <option value="H">High (H)</option>
                    </select>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="flex gap-3 mt-4">
                <button
                    id="generate-btn"
                    class="px-5 py-2 bg-blue-600 text-white rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-700 text-sm font-medium"
                >
                    Generate QR Code
                </button>
                <button
                    id="download-btn"
                    class="px-5 py-2 bg-gray-200 text-gray-800 rounded-lg hover:bg-gray-300 text-sm font-medium"
                    disabled
                >
                    Download PNG
                </button>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-8 flex justify-center">
            <div
                id="qr-output"
                class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 hidden"
            >
                <img id="qr-image" alt="Generated QR Code" class="max-w-full" />
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <!-- SEO Content (800+ words) -->
    <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-16 prose prose-gray">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">About This QR Code Generator</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            This free online QR code generator lets you create QR codes for any
            text, URL, phone number, or message. Customize the size and error
            correction level, then download your QR code as a PNG image. No
            signup, no watermark, completely free.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            QR codes have become part of daily life — restaurant menus, business
            cards, product packaging, event tickets, and even Wi-Fi sharing.
            This tool makes creating one as simple as typing text and clicking a
            button. Everything runs in your browser, so nothing is uploaded to
            any server.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">How to Use</h3>
        <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
            <li>Enter the text or URL you want to encode.</li>
            <li>Choose the size (in pixels) and error correction level.</li>
            <li>Click "Generate QR Code" to create your QR code.</li>
            <li>Click "Download PNG" to save the image to your device.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">Why Use This Tool?</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
            <li>
                <strong>Instant generation:</strong> Type text, click a button, download.
                No waiting.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>No signup:</strong> No account, no email, no verification.
                Just use it.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>No watermark:</strong> The QR code you download is clean —
                no logos, no branding.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Privacy first:</strong> Everything runs in your browser. Your
                text never leaves your device.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Free with no limits:</strong> Generate as many QR codes as
                you want, as often as you want.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">What Can You Encode?</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
            <li>
                <strong>Website URLs:</strong> Link to your site, a product page,
                or a YouTube video.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Plain text:</strong> A message, coupon code, or instruction.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Phone numbers:</strong> Scanning opens the dialer with the
                number pre-filled.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Email addresses:</strong> Opens a pre-addressed email draft.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Wi-Fi credentials:</strong> Auto-connect to a network (requires
                Wi-Fi format).
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>vCards:</strong> Full contact information saved directly to
                the phone.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Payment links:</strong> PayPal, Venmo, UPI, and other apps.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Geographic coordinates:</strong> Opens a specific location
                in Maps.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">Common Use Cases</h3>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">1. Restaurant Menus</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Place a QR code on each table so customers can view the menu without
            handling paper. Updating the menu is as simple as changing the URL —
            no reprinting needed.
        </p>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">2. Business Cards</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Add a QR code to your business card that opens your LinkedIn
            profile, portfolio, or a vCard. Recipients scan once and have your
            contact info saved instantly.
        </p>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">3. Product Packaging</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Include a QR code for warranty registration, tutorials, or exclusive
            content. This turns physical packaging into a digital touchpoint.
        </p>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">4. Event Ticketing</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            QR codes on tickets allow quick scanning at the entrance — no manual
            name checks, no delays.
        </p>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">5. Wi-Fi Sharing</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            For cafés, hotels, and offices: place a QR code on the wall that
            connects guests to Wi-Fi automatically. No more passing around
            passwords.
        </p>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">6. Marketing Campaigns</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Print QR codes on flyers, posters, and brochures that link to
            landing pages, discount codes, or app downloads.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">
            Understanding Error Correction Levels
        </h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Error correction level determines how much damage a QR code can
            sustain and still be readable. Higher levels make the code denser
            but more robust.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
            <li>
                <strong>Low (L):</strong> 7% of the code can be damaged. Smallest
                file size, best for clean digital displays.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Medium (M):</strong> 15% damage tolerance. Good default for
                most uses.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Quartile (Q):</strong> 25% damage tolerance. Good for printed
                materials that might get scratched.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>High (H):</strong> 30% damage tolerance. Best for adding logos
                or using on rough surfaces.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">A Worked Example</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Here's what happens when you generate a QR code for a URL:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
            <li>
                <strong>Input:</strong>
                <code>https://toolsvibe.online/tools/</code>
            </li>
            <li><strong>Size:</strong> 300 × 300 pixels</li>
            <li><strong>Error correction:</strong> Medium (M)</li>
            <li>
                <strong>Output:</strong> A PNG image, roughly 3–5 KB, ready to print
                or share
            </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mt-4 mb-4">
            When scanned with an iPhone or Android camera, the code opens the
            URL instantly. No app needed.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">
            Frequently Asked Questions
        </h3>
        <div class="space-y-4 mt-3">
            <div>
                <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                    What is error correction level?
                </h4>
                <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                    Error correction level determines how much damage a QR code
                    can sustain and still be readable. Higher levels (H) make
                    the QR code more robust but denser. For most uses, Medium
                    (M) is a good balance.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">Do QR codes expire?</h4>
                <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                    No, QR codes generated here are static and never expire.
                    They encode your text directly, so they'll work forever — as
                    long as the destination URL stays live.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                    Do I need a special app to scan QR codes?
                </h4>
                <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                    No. Modern iPhones and Android phones scan QR codes with the
                    default camera app. Just point and tap. Older devices may
                    need a third-party app.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                    What's the maximum data a QR code can store?
                </h4>
                <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                    Up to 4,296 alphanumeric characters, 7,089 numeric
                    characters, or 2,953 bytes of binary data — though shorter
                    data makes for easier scanning.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                    Why won't my phone scan this QR code?
                </h4>
                <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                    Common causes: dirty camera lens, low lighting, code too
                    small, low contrast, or a damaged print. Try cleaning the
                    lens and moving the phone 10–15 cm back.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">Is this tool free?</h4>
                <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                    Yes, completely free with no limits, no signup, and no
                    watermark.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Related Tools & Guides -->
    <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-16">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Related Tools</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-10">
            <a
                href="/tools/image-compressor/"
                class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
            >
                <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">Image Compressor</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                    Compress JPG, PNG, and WebP images.
                </p>
            </a>
            <a
                href="/tools/password-generator/"
                class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
            >
                <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">Password Generator</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                    Create strong, random passwords.
                </p>
            </a>
            <a
                href="/tools/unit-converter/"
                class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
            >
                <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">Unit Converter</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                    Convert length, weight, and temperature.
                </p>
            </a>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Related Guides</h2>
        <div class="space-y-3">
            <a
                href="/blog/what-is-qr-code/"
                class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
            >
                <h3 class="font-medium">
                    What is a QR Code and How Does It Work?
                </h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Complete guide to QR codes.</p>
            </a>
            <a
                href="/blog/scan-qr-code-iphone/"
                class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
            >
                <h3 class="font-medium">How to Scan a QR Code on iPhone</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                    Step-by-step iPhone scanning guide.
                </p>
            </a>
            <a
                href="/blog/scan-qr-code-android/"
                class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
            >
                <h3 class="font-medium">How to Scan a QR Code on Android</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                    Complete guide for Android users.
                </p>
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <script>
        import QRCode from "qrcode";

        const input = document.getElementById("qr-input") as HTMLInputElement;
        const sizeSelect = document.getElementById(
            "qr-size",
        ) as HTMLSelectElement;
        const levelSelect = document.getElementById(
            "qr-level",
        ) as HTMLSelectElement;
        const generateBtn = document.getElementById("generate-btn")!;
        const downloadBtn = document.getElementById(
            "download-btn",
        ) as HTMLButtonElement;
        const output = document.getElementById("qr-output")!;
        const qrImage = document.getElementById("qr-image") as HTMLImageElement;

        async function generateQR() {
            const text = input.value.trim();
            if (!text) {
                alert("Please enter some text or URL.");
                return;
            }

            const size = parseInt(sizeSelect.value);
            const level = levelSelect.value as "L" | "M" | "Q" | "H";

            try {
                const dataUrl = await QRCode.toDataURL(text, {
                    width: size,
                    margin: 2,
                    errorCorrectionLevel: level,
                });
                qrImage.src = dataUrl;
                output.classList.remove("hidden");
                downloadBtn.disabled = false;
            } catch (err) {
                alert("Failed to generate QR code. Please try again.");
            }
        }

        generateBtn.addEventListener("click", generateQR);

        downloadBtn.addEventListener("click", () => {
            if (!qrImage.src) return;
            const link = document.createElement("a");
            link.href = qrImage.src;
            link.download = "qrcode.png";
            link.click();
        });

        input.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => {
            if (e.key === "Enter") generateQR();
        });
    </script>

    <script
        type="application/ld+json"
        set:html={JSON.stringify({
            "@context": "https://schema.org",
            "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
            name: "QR Code Generator",
            applicationCategory: "UtilityApplication",
            operatingSystem: "Any",
            description:
                "Free online QR code generator. Create custom QR codes for any text or URL and download as PNG.",
            offers: {
                "@type": "Offer",
                price: "0",
                priceCurrency: "USD",
            },
        })}
    />

    <script
        type="application/ld+json"
        set:html={JSON.stringify({
            "@context": "https://schema.org",
            "@type": "FAQPage",
            mainEntity: [
                {
                    "@type": "Question",
                    name: "What is error correction level?",
                    acceptedAnswer: {
                        "@type": "Answer",
                        text: "Error correction level determines how much damage a QR code can sustain and still be readable. Higher levels (H) make the QR code more robust but denser.",
                    },
                },
                {
                    "@type": "Question",
                    name: "Do QR codes expire?",
                    acceptedAnswer: {
                        "@type": "Answer",
                        text: "No, QR codes generated here are static and never expire. They encode your text directly.",
                    },
                },
                {
                    "@type": "Question",
                    name: "Is this tool free?",
                    acceptedAnswer: {
                        "@type": "Answer",
                        text: "Yes, completely free with no limits, no signup, and no watermark.",
                    },
                },
            ],
        })}
    />
</Layout>
